{
  "schema": "vellum.parity.corpus.v1",
  "corpus_id": "pulp-platform-android-emulator-v1",
  "description": "G7 Android, Pulp vs Pulp: the debug APK `./gradlew assembleDebug` builds (android.yml android-build; arm64-v8a, PULP_ENABLE_GPU=ON without an Android Skia slice, so the CPU canvas) installed on an API 35 google_apis arm64-v8a emulator started with -no-audio -read-only, its PulpActivity launched, and the app's log read after a settle time. This is the android.yml android-emulator-test recipe, which also requires the process to stay up and no fatal exception to be logged. The JNI contract is static: every Kotlin `external fun` and Java `native` method under android/app/src/main (65, listed by evidence/G5-G7/jni_natives.py from the same checkout) plus JNI_OnLoad must be a dynamic export of libpulp.so; Pulp registers no natives at run time (no RegisterNatives call).",
  "declared_gaps": [
    {
      "row": "host checks 3-5 (render, editor lifecycle, two instances)",
      "reason": "Android has no plug-in format; the app is the product. This lane proves load, JNI bridge, activity start and survival; it does not drive the UI or render audio offline."
    },
    {
      "row": "column B",
      "reason": "Android Skia has no prebuilt slice; the APK falls back to the CPU canvas."
    }
  ],
  "declared_exceptions": [],
  "cases": [
